@startuml
title Cadastro e login de cliente (FF-1)

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Cliente
boundary "API REST" as API
control "Usuario Service" as US
control "Auth Service" as AS
database "Banco de Dados" as DB

== Cadastrar usuario (com credencial) ==

Cliente -> API: POST /usuarios\n{nome, email, senha}
API -> US: cadastrar(nome, email, senha)
US -> DB: BEGIN
US -> DB: INSERT usuarios (uuid, nome, email)

alt Email ja cadastrado
    DB --> US: conflito (uq_usuarios_email)
    US -> DB: ROLLBACK
    US --> API: conflito
    API --> Cliente: 409 Conflict
else Email livre
    US -> DB: INSERT users\n(username=email,\npassword=bcrypt(senha),\nrole=ROLE_CLIENT,\nusuario_id=usuarios.id)
    DB --> US: ok
    US -> DB: COMMIT
    US --> API: usuario criado
    API --> Cliente: 201 Created\n{id: "usuario_uuid"}
end

note over US, DB
  usuarios e users sao criados na mesma transacao.
  users.usuario_id referencia usuarios.id (1:1).
  A senha nunca e devolvida na resposta.
end note

== Login do cliente ==

Cliente -> API: POST /auth/login\n{username: email, password: senha}
API -> AS: login(username, password)
AS -> DB: SELECT users WHERE username = email
DB --> AS: User (role=ROLE_CLIENT)
AS -> AS: passwordEncoder.matches?\njwtService.generateToken(email, ROLE_CLIENT)

alt Credenciais invalidas
    AS --> API: BadCredentialsException
    API --> Cliente: 401 Unauthorized
else Credenciais validas
    AS --> API: {token, tokenType, expiresInMs}
    API --> Cliente: 200 OK\n{token, tokenType:"Bearer",\nexpiresInMs}
end

note over Cliente, API
  JWT: subject=email, claim role=ROLE_CLIENT.
  O admin continua logando com username="admin".
end note

note over DB
  Esquema (migration V4):
  ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN username TYPE VARCHAR(255);
  ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN usuario_id BIGINT REFERENCES usuarios(id);
  CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uq_users_usuario
    ON users (usuario_id) WHERE usuario_id IS NOT NULL;
end note

@enduml
